///! value: the data model the text encodings read into and write from.
///!
///! `Value` is a tagged union over six kinds: `Null`, `Bool`, `Number`,
///! `String`, `Array` and `Object`. A `Number` keeps the kind its source
///! wrote (`Int`, `UInt` or `Float`), so an integer read as `42` is written
///! back as `42`; `as_f64()` converts on request. An `Object` keeps its
///! members in insertion order and finds one by key in O(1) on average.
///!
///! A value of a Cryo type is written as a `Value` through `ToValue` and
///! read back from one through `FromValue`; a type gets both from
///! `with [ToValue, FromValue]`. A refused read is a `ValueDecodeError` naming
///! where in the value it was and what was expected there.
///!
///! Each format reads and writes the model through a type of its own
///! module: `std::encoding::json::Json::parse(text)` and
///! `Json::to_text(&value)`.
///!
///! Sub-modules:
///!   - `model`   - `Value`, `Number`, `Object`, `Extract`
///!   - `convert` - `ToValue`, `FromValue`, `ValueDecodeError`

namespace std::encoding::value;

module {
    encoding::value::model;
    encoding::value::convert;
}

export std::encoding::value::model::{ Extract, Number, Object, Value };
export std::encoding::value::convert::{ FromValue, ToValue, ValueDecodeError };
